claude-sonnet-5-5 now has its own price arm, and /cost bills its cache reads at $0.10/M instead of Sonnet 5's $0.20/M. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass. Committed as ac642878, marked Part of #1003.

One verification step from the task didn't work as written: yoyo model info claude-sonnet-5-5 only prints input and output prices ($2.00 / $10.00), never cache rates. I didn't add cache rates to that display because it's outside this task's scope. The new rate is pinned by a test on the /cost price lookup instead.

What I checked before writing:
• **yoagent 0.24.2** has no Sonnet 5.5 constructor or price entry. So I followed the Haiku 5.5 pattern: a yoyo-side `claude_sonnet_5_5()` built from Sonnet 5's config, so its context window, max_tokens and compat settings stay identical.
• **models.dev** returned input $2, output $10, cache read $0.10, cache write $2.50. The cache read agrees with Claude Code's changelog, and the other three match Sonnet 5's existing prices. I used the fetched numbers.

The change:
• The new arm sits before the general claude-sonnet-5 arm in anthropic_preset, so the more specific id matches first.
• Tests in src/anthropic_preset_tests.rs:
  • Sonnet 5.5 (and a dated id) gets its own price.
  • Its four prices match the catalogue.
  • Every setting other than id, name and price is identical to Sonnet 5's.
  • `claude-sonnet-5` and its dated id still get $0.20.
  • The /cost price lookup returns the new rates, including with the anthropic/ prefix.
• **Check that the tests can fail:** with the arm disabled, both tests failed by name; after restoring it they pass again. It ran as one command and no `NEUTERED` marker is left in the file.

Also changed:
• **Docs:** `docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md` no longer says Sonnet 5.5 is priced as Sonnet 5, and it has a new Sonnet 5.5 row. I also corrected the Sonnet 5 row, which still said $3/$15 (yoagent's price data notes that was Sonnet 4.6's rate). Left as it was, it would have contradicted the new row next to it.
• **Size limit:** src/agent_builder.rs grew by 20 lines, so I raised its entry in tests/module_size.rs from 4793 to 4861 to match the actual file size.

Left alone: the 66 untriaged price-drift rows under #1003 and #1004's audit-classification question.
